ah Valley. Although the falls flow powerfully during the snow melt of late spring and early summer, it is usually a trickle by autumn, occasionally drying up completely during poor snow years.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tokopah_Falls","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","attribution":"Wikipedia"},"photos":[],"street":null},{"id":"node/888301283","name":"Chagoopa Falls","kind":"waterfall","lon":-118.41505,"lat":36.46925,"ele_m":2134.0,"wikidata":"Q120196814","url":null},{"id":"node/7900152238","name":"Lion Rock","kind":"peak","lon":-118.54207,"lat":36.58244,"ele_m":3767.0,"wikidata":"Q107144008","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lion_Rock_(California)","tour":5,"summary":{"extract":"Lion Rock is a 12,360-foot-elevation (3,770-meter) mountain summit located along the Great Western Divide of the Sierra Nevada mountain range, in Tulare County of northern California. It is situated in Sequoia National Park, one mile northeast of Mount Stewart, and one mile southwest of Triple Divide Peak. Topographic relief is significant as the west aspect rises 3,145 feet above Tamarack Lake in 1.5 mile, and the north aspect rises 1,355 feet above Lion Lake in 0.38 mile. Lion Rock ranks as the 311th highest summit in California.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lion_Rock_(California)","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","attribution":"Wikipedia"},"photos":[],"street":null},{"id":"node/1751223608","name":"Moro Rock","kind":"peak","lon":-118.76511,"lat":36.54409,"ele_m":2050.0,"wikidata":"Q2156029","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moro_Rock","tour":1,"summary":{"extract":"Moro Rock is a granite dome rock formation in Sequoia National Park, California, United States. It is located in the center of the park, at the head of Moro Creek, between Giant Forest and Crescent Meadow. A stairway, designed by the National Park Service and built in 1931, is cut into and poured onto the rock, so that visitors can hike to the top. The view from the rock encompasses much of the Park, including the Great Western Divide. Use of this trail is discouraged during thunderstorms and when it is snowing.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moro_Rock","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","attribution":"Wikipedia"},"photos":[{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/17_23_443_highway.jpg/960px-17_23_443_highway.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:17_23_443_highway.jpg","dist_m":18,"width":640,"height":433,"license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","artist":"Dsdugan"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/View_from_Moro_Rock_-_Sequoia_National_Park%2C_Tulare_County%2C_California%2C_USA_-_August_1995.jpg/960px-View_from_Moro_Rock_-_Sequoia_National_Park%2C_Tulare_County%2C_California%2C_USA_-_August_1995.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_from_Moro_Rock_-_Sequoia_National_Park,_Tulare_County,_California,_USA_-_August_1995.jpg","dist_m":19,"width":640,"height":427,"license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","artist":"Giorgio Galeotti"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Moro_Rock_%2832050607131%29.jpg/960px-Moro_Rock_%2832050607131%29.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Moro_Rock_(32050607131).jpg","dist_m":22,"width":640,"height":960,"license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","artist":"m01229 from USA"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Stairway_going_down_at_the_Moro_Rock_Trail_-_Sequoia_National_Park_%2827713795786%29.jpg/960px-Stairway_going_down_at_the_Moro_Rock_Trail_-_Sequoia_National_Park_%2827713795786%29.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stairway_going_down_at_the_Moro_Rock_Trail_-_Sequoia_National_Park_(27713795786).jpg","dist_m":22,"width":640,"height":427,"license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","artist":"m01